-- title:
--   Commute GHalf Sandwich Prefix Second Slice Left Lift
-- statement:
--   **Prefixing a second slice effect preserves the operator relation.**
--
--   Let $(m,q,d)$ have a field model, let $\psi_{AB}$ be a bipartite quantum state, let $F$ be a slice-indexed polynomial family, and let $r\in\mathbb N$. Let $A$ and $B$ be operator families on a slice question together with an $r$-tuple of tail points, with outcomes consisting of one completed slice outcome and one completed-outcome tail tuple. Assume
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDOpRel}_{\psi_{AB},\,\operatorname{Unif}(\mathcal Q\times\mathbb{F}_q^r)}(A,B;\delta).
--   $$
--
--   Write $\mathsf P_r(F)$ for the family obtained by adjoining the completed slice effect corresponding to the second distinguished slice coordinate on the left register, and by applying the canonical question and outcome reindexing to the move-chain spaces. Then
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDOpRel}_{\psi_{AB},\,\operatorname{Unif}(\mathsf{MoveQ}_r)}
--   \left(\mathsf P_r(F,A),\mathsf P_r(F,B);\delta\right).
--   $$
--
--   Here $\mathcal Q$ is the slice-question space, and $\mathsf{MoveQ}_r$ is the corresponding move-chain question space. The lift is used to prefix the second slice factor in the post-move flat-step comparison.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.commuteGHalfSandwich_prefixSecondSliceLeftLift`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
